    - target: {fileID: 6220877059410649044, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "The clover shader uses one single channel texture to save memory. Color
        is generated by lerping between a bright color and a dark color using the
        texture. Position is used to give each instance a color variation.\r\nThe
        Distance Mask is calculated in the vertex shader to save performance and
        then passed to the pixel shader where it\u2019s combined with the texture
        and some screen space noise. These elements are passed into the Fade Transition
        node which makes the mesh dissolve between the Clip Offset and Clip Distance
        values.\r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6539571802878535714, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'm_Materials.Array.data[0]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: -876546973899608171, guid: 2dccc62e34304c145897d5807ed8a706, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 6627578990819076097, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_IsActive
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6653079432833169106, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'm_Materials.Array.data[0]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: -876546973899608171, guid: 2dccc62e34304c145897d5807ed8a706, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 7542701914138946096, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'm_Materials.Array.data[0]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: -876546973899608171, guid: 2dccc62e34304c145897d5807ed8a706, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 8033412307876056146, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "If the decals aren't rendering here, add the Decal Renderer Feature
        to your project's Renderer asset.\n\nDecals allow you to apply local material
        modifications to specific places in the world. You might think of things
        like applying graffiti tags to a wall or scattering fallen leaves below a
        tree. But decals can be used for a lot more. In these examples, we see decals
        making things look wet, making surfaces appear to have flowing water across
        them, projecting water caustics, and blending specific materials onto other
        objects.\r\n\r\nDecals are available to use in both HDRP and URP, but they
        need to be enabled in both render pipelines. To use decals, see the documentation
        in both HDRP and URP.\r"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8420169003435983860, guid: 97bd81fbbace2cf42810785102781490, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'm_Materials.Array.data[0]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: -876546973899608171, guid: 2dccc62e34304c145897d5807ed8a706, type: 3}
